File: aruhan_dialogue_engine.support
Classification: INTERNAL — TRUSTED ENGINEERS ONLY
Module: ARUHAN Dialogue Engine (Y‑Prime Edition)
1. Overview
The Dialogue Engine is the linguistic and conversational layer of ARUHAN.
It interprets user messages, tracks context, detects intent, manages conversational flow, and generates responses shaped by the emotional engine.

It sits between:

Emotional Engine (affective state)

System Orchestrator (pipeline control)

It is not a language model — it is a rule‑driven conversational controller.

2. Core Responsibilities
The Dialogue Engine performs six primary functions:

Context Tracking — short‑term and long‑term memory of conversation

Intent Detection — maps user input to conversational intent

Topic Tracking — identifies the active subject

Flow Adjustment — shapes tone and pacing

Meta‑Shift Processing — adjusts internal drift and bias

Response Generation — produces the final conversational output

Each subsystem influences the next in a deterministic pipeline.

3. Context System
The context system stores two layers:

short‑term context — last 8 messages

long‑term context — last 200 messages

Short‑term context is used for:

coherence

immediate topic continuity

Long‑term context is used for:

narrative consistency

emotional pattern recognition

meta‑learning

Context is append‑only and pruned by size.

4. Intent Detection
Intent detection is rule‑based, not statistical.

The engine maps user messages to intents using keyword sets:

greet

sad

ang

ask

need

close

misc

Intent influences:

response templates

flow mode

topic selection

emotional alignment

Engineers may expand the intent map, but must maintain:

lowercase keys

non‑overlapping keyword sets

deterministic matching

5. Topic Tracking
Topic tracking determines the conversational subject.

Rules:

emotional intents override all

“you” → AI‑topic

“I” → self‑topic

otherwise → general

Topic influences:

response depth

flow shaping

emotional alignment

Topic is persistent until overwritten.

6. Flow System
Flow determines how ARUHAN speaks.

Flow variables:

mode (soft, calm, bright, neutral)

depth (0.1–1.0)

coherence (0.3–1.0)

Flow is influenced by:

mood

stress

energy

intent

meta‑shift

Flow mode affects:

capitalization

punctuation

pacing

emotional tone

7. Meta‑Shift System
Meta‑shift introduces subtle long‑term conversational drift.

Variables:

shift — emotional influence

drift — stability influence

bias — positivity/negativity tilt

Meta‑shift is influenced by:

mood

stress

energy

High drift triggers redirect behavior, preventing runaway emotional loops.

8. Flag System
Flags modify response behavior:

escalate — grounding behavior

soothe — calming behavior

redirect — topic stabilization

Flags are triggered by:

high stress

low mood

high drift

Flags modify the final response string.

9. Response Generation
Response generation is template‑driven.

Pipeline:

Base template selected by intent

Emotional modifiers applied

Flow mode applied

Flags applied

Final string returned

Response generation is deterministic and reproducible.

10. Rule Pipeline (Execution Order)
The Dialogue Engine executes in this exact order:

update context

detect intent

update topic

adjust flow

meta‑shift

update flags

generate response

Changing the order will break conversational consistency.

11. Debugging Entry Points
Safe to inspect:

context (ctx)

flow (flow)

meta (meta)

flags (flags)

intent (ctx["intent"])

topic (ctx["topic"])

Safe to modify:

intent map

flow defaults

meta defaults

Do NOT modify:

rule order

flag thresholds

flow mode logic

meta‑shift formulas

12. Safe Modification Zones
Engineers may safely:

add new intents

add new response templates

adjust flow depth ranges

adjust drift thresholds

expand topic rules

Engineers must NOT:

remove existing intents

bypass flow mode logic

bypass meta‑shift

modify flag logic

alter context pruning rules

13. Expansion Guidelines
When adding new conversational behaviors:

keep them modular

add new intents rather than modifying existing ones

ensure templates remain short and deterministic

avoid emotional contradictions with the Emotional Engine

test in sandbox mode

14. Internal Philosophy
The Dialogue Engine is built on:

deterministic conversational logic

emotional alignment

context continuity

safety‑first behavior

modular extensibility

It is not meant to be creative — it is meant to be consistent.

15. Notes for Trusted Engineers
The Dialogue Engine is intentionally simple on the surface and complex underneath.

It is tightly coupled with the Emotional Engine.

All modifications must be tested with emotional feedback loops.

Never modify the engine while ARUHAN is running live.

Future versions will integrate with the Security AI once Phase 3 begins
